        "id": 1000205
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-07T19:53:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "why is this global? If there are multiple tipc instances, a handle shared with one instance should not be accessible to a different instance.",
      "revId": "5d0c105ebfec56e16bc01c3500d5b28db31467d6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4c50d578_3b205698",
        "filename": "drivers/trusty/trusty-ipc.c",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 175,
      "author": {
        "id": 1416371
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-07T21:58:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I made the structure global because the handle namespace is over our communication with the SPM, not specific tipc devices. If we evolve to a platform where the SPM supports multi-way sharing, this will be a lot easier to extend than a per-tipc version. as we can just change the dev pointer to be an array of dev pointers.\n\nThis is safe to be global because the only thing done with these shared handles is to release them upon confirmation from FF-A. The worst thing a misbehaving tipc instance can trick us into doing is asking the FF-A if a handle can be reclaimed spuriously, which is already properly handled.",
      "parentUuid": "57a01582_19b26d7d",
      "revId": "5d0c105ebfec56e16bc01c3500d5b28db31467d6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0d4714ae_08748cda",
        "filename": "drivers/trusty/trusty-ipc.c",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 175,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000205
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-07T22:36:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think we should rely on there being only one instance of the SPM either. The FF-A protocol could be used to communicate with other entities as well.",
      "parentUuid": "4c50d578_3b205698",
      "revId": "5d0c105ebfec56e16bc01c3500d5b28db31467d6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8c568930_bd86127b",
        "filename": "drivers/trusty/trusty-ipc.c",
